efkbgfx on Effekseer 1.80 inside the engine's bgfx build.

- Effekseer 1.80: RenderStateBase's members are next_/active_, the model vertex has UV2 (TEXCOORD1), sprite lit and
  distortion shaders apply the tangent's handedness (Tangent.w), create_texture_2d takes the external-handle argument.
- Shaders are embedded by the engine's build for both backends (storm_efk_shaders.hpp) instead of upstream's
  shader_load callback. GLSL: no HLSL (T)0 struct casts, sampler parameters are sampler2D. The instanced arrays are 10
  wide (MaxInstanced, as Effekseer's own GL renderer on GLES) instead of 40 in the shaders and 20 in the renderer.
- Textures come from the host (CreateTextureFromHandle, ReplaceTextureHandle); the renderer's CreateTexture makes only
  Effekseer's 1x1 proxy textures. Upstream's texture callbacks and its material (.efkmat) code go: efkbgfx has no
  material shader generator, the host reports such nodes.
- No scene background or depth copy: distortion nodes are skipped by Effekseer, soft particles are drawn hard.
- mirror_winding: a projection that flips Y (bottom-left-origin targets) swaps the culling winding. Draw calls are
  counted for Effekseer's statistics; the view is set per frame (SetViewId).

